From 1b40f4721efa0310d337db69f1d1759951618c7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Samuel=20Carre=C3=B1o?= <soyminero11yt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:36:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AModule: bring back menu/menu-file/menu-actions on GTK4 with
 a PopoverMenu

GTK4 has no GtkMenu, so the port silently ignored the "menu" option and
buttons configured with a menu-file did nothing. Parse the documented GTK3
builder format (GtkMenu with GtkMenuItem / GtkSeparatorMenuItem children)
with Glib::Markup, build a sectioned Gio::Menu backed by a SimpleActionGroup
("menu.<id>" runs the matching menu-actions command through forkExec) and
show it in a Gtk::PopoverMenu parented to the module widget on the configured
event. The popover is unparented when the widget is destroyed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
